    "bodyText": "Two Things That Don't Matter Very Much   Its okay to support gay marriage and less government. It is okay to support religious freedom and be an atheist. It is okay to be an atheist and not be a communist. It is okay to be pro-choice and be a Christian. You don't have to believe something because your particular party or religion doesn't condone it. You are not your political party or your religion.  These are tools you use to deal with different cards dealt by life. Everyone has there views but just because you are apart of something doesn't mean you have to be everything that idolizes this particular group. Stop fracking kidding yourself, you can support anything you want.\n\nI'm sick and tired of seeing people being so hard headed about these groups they are apart of. Its like you follow everything these groups say because you're in with that group, it doesn't work like that. You can have you own ideas, its okay the wolves aren't always watching. Your not going to die because you didn't support some stupid bill being passed. If you don't support the bill then open your mouth and talk about it. If you support the bill open your mouth. Its very simple follow your feelings and morals about your views and you will be fine.\n\nPolitical parties should die in a fiery pit of death. Political parties are proprietary. They try to throw a few people in a small group. Its like trying to take the six kingdoms and putting them into two. It just can't work like that. In todays society we are grid locked into a certain way of views and thoughts. I don't know about you but I was taught ideas mean more then anything in the world. Actually I know a man who said something similar to this. “Ideas are very important to the shaping of society. In fact, they are more powerful than bombings or armies or guns. And this is because ideas are capable of spreading without limit. They are behind all the choices we make. They can transform the world in a way that governments and armies cannot. Fighting for liberty with ideas makes more sense to me than fighting with guns or politics or political power. With ideas, we can make real change that lasts.” Ron Paul.\n\nWe have gotten so far from where we started. We keep indoctrinating are children into sheep herds. Can you expect a sheep to look outside of the field they spend so much time in? No you cant! Think of the field as peoples narrow frame of ideals. “Sheep” will have tunnel vision and be locked into there indoctrinated beliefs until death. Think out side the box. The greatest minds of history have never lived inside the box of normalcy. Its okay to live outside the box, its not going to kill you. You will survive. I hope someone stands up and does something about this world. In the words of John McClane “Do you know what you get for being a hero? Nothin'. You get shot at. Pat on the back, blah blah blah. 'Attaboy.' You get divorced... Your wife can't remember your last name, kids don't want to talk to you... You get to eat a lot of meals by yourself. Trust me kid, nobody wants to be that guy. (I do this) because there is nobody else to do it right now. Believe me if there was somebody else to do it, I would let them do it. There's not, so (I'm) doing it. That's what makes you that guy”.\n\nIts time to rise up and support what you believe. Whats going on in this country is more important then your job. More important then your slutty girl friend you just knocked up. You're looking at the small picture not the bigger picture. If this country and world gets worse, might as well kill that baby yourself because you will be raising it in a world you will regret bringing it into. Read, watch, listen and develop your own ideals. Your ideas will change the world!",
